  "body": "Stacked on #2418 (merge #2418 first)\n\n## What changed\n\nTilted height planes now use the operation frame and the shared `fold_height` resolver.\nThe rectangle spans the stock in local XY.\nIts corners and label anchors pass through `TiltedFrame::to_world`.\nHeight echoes and viewport labels state the local distance along the tool axis.\nDraft tilt edits update these values before Apply.\nInvalid tilts hide the planes and show the existing named refusal.\n`operation::region_z` uses the same folded height.\nUntilted planes and text retain their existing behavior.\n\nThe original stack used parent head `3e62cea0a`.\nThis branch also includes the requested pocket island and depth validation fixes from parent head `302b097254569c239d5d5e3f28ff06625080b92c`.\nThe display changes address #2416.\nThe decision record is `docs/decisions/2416-tilted-height-display.md`.\n\n## Cause\n\nThe display resolved heights as setup Z and drew horizontal stock-XY rectangles.\nIt did not read the tilted tool axis.\nOn the asymmetric test stock, the correct clearance is 21 along the axis.\nThe old display placed a clearance corner at local height -5.\nThe old region read returned 10 instead of the fold coordinate 14.\n\n## Tests before review fixes\n\nSeven pins in `egui_app::heights_tests` failed before this fix:\n\n- `tilted_height_planes_use_tool_axis_and_local_stock_corners`\n- `tilted_height_echoes_use_tool_axis_on_asymmetric_stock`\n- `invalid_draft_tilt_hides_height_planes_and_names_the_missing_direction`\n- `tilted_height_region_level_uses_the_same_fold`\n- `tilted_height_echoes_follow_an_unapplied_tilt_edit`\n- `tilted_fixed_height_echoes_keep_the_generation_origin_shift`\n- `tilted_height_labels_show_local_axis_distance`\n\nAll 12 tests in the height suite pass.\nThe unchanged-code runs used the parent head before the #2416 fix.\n\nTen mutation checks failed, then passed after restoration:\n\n- Restore the old region-height resolver.\n- Restore the old plane rendering code.\n- Restore the old height echo and its page context.\n- Replace local stock bounds with world bounds.\n- Remove the origin-Z shift from plane placement.\n- Remove draft tilt forwarding.\n- Remove the invalid-frame guard from height planes.\n- Remove the invalid-frame guard from the region-height read.\n- Remove the invalid-frame guard from the height echo.\n- Restore the old viewport label value.\n\nThe old region mutation retained the parent resolver adapter so the stack could compile.\nThe mutated region function matched upstream/main.\n\n`cargo xtask gate quick --base upstream/main` passed: 253 steps, zero failures.\nClippy then requested an equivalent closure simplification.\nAll 12 height tests passed again after that change.\n`cargo clippy -p camcraft-app -p camcraft-ui --all-targets -- -D warnings` passed on the final code.\n\nEffort: high for the review fixes. No escalation.\n\n## Review fixes\n\nHead: `26f2162873f3fd882ea35f5c1c0cf609c51dc073`.\n\n`cargo xtask gate quick --base upstream/main` passed on this head.\nResult: 253 steps, 3,198 tests passed, 27 ignored, zero failures.\n`cargo clippy -j 6 -p camcraft-app -p camcraft-ui --all-targets -- -D warnings` passed with zero warnings.\n\nBoth pocket island ladders now use the folded tool-axis heights.\nThe pins are `tilted_whole_model_reference_pocket_preserves_part_islands` and `tilted_stock_reference_pocket_preserves_part_islands`.\nRestoring the old ladder heights makes each pin fail with 16 gouge warnings.\n\nDepth validation now uses the checked tilt frame and the folded resolver.\nThe pins are `tilted_mixed_reference_depth_is_accepted_on_creation`, `tilted_mixed_reference_depth_is_accepted_on_editing`, and `tilted_upward_mixed_reference_depth_is_refused_on_creation_and_editing`.\nRestoring the old resolver makes all three pins fail.\nAll eight `tilt_heights` tests pass after restoration.\nAn independent agent also ran this suite and confirmed eight passes.\n\nThe display cache retains local bounds and resolved heights for unchanged inputs.\nIts key includes geometry allocations, placements, entity membership, setup definitions, source, height, and draft tilt.\nGeneration, verification, and posting do not read this cache.\nSeven `height_memo::tests` pins cover unchanged frames and changed inputs.\nThe caller pin is `display_callers_fill_the_cache_then_reuse_their_geometry_reads`.\nThe frame pin is `unchanged_viewport_and_height_rows_do_not_resolve_geometry_again`.\nThree mutations compile and fail: bypass the cache, restore the uncached height echo, and bypass the bounds cache.\nAll seven pins pass after each restoration.\n\nThe before/after screenshots below use the real GPU renderer and the production Heights page.\nThe PNG files exist only on the fork's images branch.\nNo screenshot, log, or temporary capture code is in this commit.\n\n## Goldens moved\n\nNone.\n`git diff --stat upstream/main -- \"*.nc\" \"*.cl\"` is empty.\n\n## Not exercised\n\nNo manual GPU viewport check or machine run.\nNo release-tier pixel snapshots or large-model frame-time measurement.\nCut-region outline and fill transforms stay unchanged.\nThe shared region-height read is pinned.\n\n## Overlaps\n\n#2418 supplies `operation::fold_height` and `resolve_params_with`.\nMerge that parent first.\n\nThese PRs touch the same file, different function; whichever merges second refreshes:\n\n- #2256: `interact.rs` changes region and highlight functions. This PR changes height planes and their labels.\n- #2134: `heights.rs` changes `missing_source`. This PR changes `region_z`.\n- #2253: `operations.rs` changes `strategy_names`. This PR changes `height_echo`.\n- #2149: `operations.rs` changes warning formatting. It also adds separate module declarations in `lib.rs`.\n- #2185 and #1330: `lib.rs` adds separate module declarations. This PR registers `height_display`.\n\nChangelog: Tilted viewport height planes and height text now use the tool axis and the shared height resolver.\n\n\n\n## Before and after screenshots\n\nThese images use the real headless `View3D` GPU renderer, the Heights page, and the viewport label function.\nThe capture harness uses the asymmetric stock from the regression tests.\nIt combines the rendered viewport and the production Heights page in one fixture view.\nThis is a headless fixture capture, not a native window capture.\nThe temporary capture code was removed after both runs passed.\n\nThe fixture uses A -90 degrees and tilt origin (2, 0, 3) mm.\nStock Y is -1..11 mm. Stock Z is -20..10 mm.\nThe heading states the intended tool-axis coordinates.\n\nBefore: parent head `3e62cea0a` shows horizontal planes and setup-Z values 20, 10, and 9.\n\n![Before: horizontal planes and setup-Z values](https://raw.githubusercontent.com/mkinney/Camcraft/2ae280f6002508d4b1a68bc50dfda042840583c5/2429/tilted-heights-before.png)\n\nAfter: the corrected display shows tilted planes and tool-axis distances 21, 11, and 10.\nThe viewport labels and the Heights rows agree.\n\n![After: tilted planes and tool-axis distances](https://raw.githubusercontent.com/mkinney/Camcraft/2ae280f6002508d4b1a68bc50dfda042840583c5/2429/tilted-heights-after.png)\n\nBoth PNG files exist only on the fork's `pr-screenshots` branch.\nImage commit: `2ae280f6002508d4b1a68bc50dfda042840583c5`.\n\nFixes #2416\n",
